---
import { PUBLISHER, REPO_HTTPS } from '../../data/canonical';
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<footer class="footer">
  <div class="footer-inner">
    <div class="footer-brand">
      <span class="footer-logo">aDNA</span>
      <p class="footer-tagline">Give your project a knowledge architecture that both humans and AI agents can navigate.</p>
    </div>
    <nav class="footer-links" aria-label="Footer navigation">
      <a href="/network">Network</a>
      <a href="/vaults">Vaults</a>
      <a href="/commons">Commons</a>
      <a href="/community">Community</a>
      {/* HAUSSMANN P3.5 — the proposal archive, in the chrome rather than only one click into
          /community. ADR-055 §7 places the surface under /community because ADR-049 caps the
          PRIMARY nav at 7 and it is at 7; the footer carries no such ceiling, and a standards
          process a reader cannot find from an arbitrary page is a process in name only. */}
      <a href="/community/proposals/">Proposals</a>
      <a href="/about">About</a>
      {/* HAUSSMANN P1.2 — both disclosure surfaces, reachable from every page. The
          canonical-properties link is load-bearing for the §7.1 clone-site defense: a reader who
          lands on a copy of this site should be one click from the list of what is genuinely ours,
          from wherever they landed. */}
      <a href="/state-of-the-network">State of the network</a>
      <a href="/canonical-properties">Canonical properties</a>
      <a href="/security">Security</a>
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
      {/* HAUSSMANN P4.3 AC5 (D11 check 14): an accessibility statement reachable only from a page
          you already knew about is not reachable. It sits beside its policy siblings, in the footer
          of every page — the one place a reader who has hit a barrier can find it from wherever
          they are. */}
      <a href="/accessibility">Accessibility</a>
      <a href="/reference/specification">Specification</a>
      <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a>
      <a href="/how">Guides</a>
      <a href="/get-started">Get Started</a>
      <a href="/changelog">Changelog</a>
      <a href="/design-system">Design system</a>
      <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>
      {/* HAUSSMANN P3.1 (machine_eye item 12): the literal string "llms" appeared ZERO times across
          every page HTML probed, so the site's one genuinely curated machine artifact was reachable
          only by an agent that already knew the convention. It belongs on the machine-artifact shelf
          the footer already keeps, beside RSS. ADR-049's cap is on PRIMARY nav (at 7); the footer is
          not primary nav, so this adds no cap pressure. */}
      <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>
      <a href={REPO_HTTPS} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
    </nav>
    {/* ⛩ HAUSSMANN P4.4b B0 / AC1 — the year is wrapped so the visual-regression mask can be TIGHT.
      * `year` is `new Date().getFullYear()` (line 3), evaluated at BUILD time and baked into every
      * page, so it is the one non-deterministic token in this line and it turns all 24 baselines red
      * on 1 January for a non-regression. Masking `.footer-copyright` wholesale would have been the
      * cheap fix and it would have swallowed the MIT licence claim — a truth claim this site makes —
      * which is exactly the OVER-MASKING hazard gate-49 is built to refuse (FINDING 4: a mask that
      * swallows a real region leaves it green forever, and masks only ever grow). One span instead. */}
    <p class="footer-copyright">&copy; <span class="footer-year">{year}</span> {PUBLISHER}. Released under the MIT License.</p>
  </div>
</footer>

<style>
  .footer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-bg-alt);
    margin-top: auto;
  }

  .footer-inner {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .footer-brand {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .footer-logo {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-heading);
  }

  .footer-tagline {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    max-width: 40ch;
  }

  .footer-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3) var(--space-6);
  }

  .footer-links a {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    transition: color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .footer-links a:hover {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .footer-copyright {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
  }
</style>
